<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Proposal 45 M4, AC4.4: THE MASTER HEAD'S FADER COMMIT IS HEARD.

  This is the assertion the plan singles out as the one that bites D9's
  WRITE-SIDE defect: a head whose slider moves and whose action never fires.
  Nothing about the widget can tell those apart, which is why the measurement
  is a RENDER and not a describeHead() string.

  THE MECHANISM UNDER TEST. SSMVMixerControl::applyVolume_ derives its commit
  address from strackpath::pathOf( mixer, &tk_ ). A system lane is NOT among
  childLinks(), so without D9's sentinel branch pathOf() answers {} for the
  master lane, which is ALSO the address of "the root itself". The fader would
  then move on screen and commit to the mixer, or to nothing at all. The head
  exists only because M4 gave the lane a ROW, so this path became reachable for
  the first time in M4 and had never been exercised.

  head-fader drives the SLIDER, not applyVolume_ directly, so the whole real
  chain runs: valueChanged -> sliderToDB -> applyVolume_ -> pathOf() ->
  set-track-volume. Calling the handler directly would skip precisely the part
  that was in doubt.

  THE CLOSED FORM. test_autosaw.wav is 0.230956 RMS and the master fader is
  moved to -6 dB, so the render must read 0.230956 x 10^(-6/20) = 0.115760.
  The band is +-3 %, which covers the fader curve's own rounding: it is an
  INTEGER control whose curve does not round-trip (sDbToFader(0.0) is tick -191,
  whose dB is +0.0625), so asking for -6 dB lands NEAR -6 dB and an exact
  assertion would be asserting the tick table rather than the commit.

  A HIDDEN LANE HAS NO HEAD, and the case says so first: head-fader is REFUSED
  before set-lane-hidden shows the lane. That is not a courtesy check; it is
  what makes the later success mean "the head exists and its fader committed"
  rather than "some path resolved somewhere".

  ONE UNDO STEP takes the level back, because the head's own handler submits an
  ordinary set-track-volume: the verb itself is not undoable and does not need
  to be.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="master_head_fader_heard">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <add-sample trackPath="0" filePath="../test_autosaw.wav" timePos="0"/>

    <!-- THE REFERENCE: a clean master, nothing touched. -->
    <render filename="head_fader_ref.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="2.0"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="head_fader_ref.wav" startFrame="24000"
                         frameCount="48000" channel="0"
                         minRms="0.2240" maxRms="0.2379"/>

    <!-- HIDDEN MEANS NO HEAD, so the gesture is refused. -->
    <head-fader trackPath="$master" db="-6" expectReject="true"/>

    <!-- Show the lane; now it has a row, and therefore a head. -->
    <set-lane-hidden trackPath="$master" hidden="0"/>
    <assert-lane-alignment rows="2"/>

    <!-- THE GESTURE: the master head's own fader, through the real chain. -->
    <head-fader trackPath="$master" db="-6"/>

    <!-- ...and it is HEARD. 0.230956 x 10^(-6/20) = 0.115760, +-3 %. -->
    <render filename="head_fader_down.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="2.0"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="head_fader_down.wav" startFrame="24000"
                         frameCount="48000" channel="0"
                         minRms="0.1123" maxRms="0.1193"/>

    <!-- The commit landed on the MASTER LANE and nowhere else: the source
         track's own fader is untouched. Without D9's sentinel branch pathOf()
         would answer {} and the write would go somewhere else entirely. -->
    <assert-track-volume trackPath="0" volumeDb="0" tolerance="0.001"/>

    <!-- ONE undo step, because the handler submitted an ordinary
         set-track-volume: the level comes back. -->
    <undo count="1"/>
    <render filename="head_fader_undo.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="2.0"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="head_fader_undo.wav" startFrame="24000"
                         frameCount="48000" channel="0"
                         minRms="0.2240" maxRms="0.2379"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <assert-track-count equals="1"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
